        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-26T11:43:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, but there is another option we can also try. For an over-long request line Netty substitutes its placeholder request (GET /bad-request HTTP/1.0, no headers), which the comment at line 140 already relies on. An over-long chunk line keeps the real request line and headers, plus the content-length the aggregator adds. So \"case TooLongHttpLineException ignored when msg.headers().isEmpty()\" would tell them apart, wouldn\u0027t it? It needs statusOf(msg, cause), called before  msg.release(). It\u0027s worth a try. And if that\u0027s too ugly, it should be fine keeping 414 and adding a one-line comment in statusOf saying that over-long chunk-size lines are reported the same way.",
      "parentUuid": "c92c651d_ead0d64a",
      "revId": "12f90e66395ae19e8872eebb8469587caa074d6c",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
